  "original_summary": "\r\nThis Java method is used to validate HTTP\\/2 headers. It takes an `H2HeaderField` object and a boolean flag `isTrailerField` as inputs. The method throws a `CompressionException` if the header is not valid.\r\n\r\nInputs and outputs of the method:\r\n- Input: `H2HeaderField header` - This is the header to be validated.\r\n- Input: `boolean isTrailerField` - This flag indicates whether the header is part of a trailer.\r\n- Output: None\r\n- Exception: `CompressionException` - This is thrown if the header is not valid.\r\n\r\nBusiness purpose:\r\nThe method is used to validate HTTP\\/2 headers. It checks if the header name starts with a colon (\":\"), which indicates a psuedo-header. If the header name is not a psuedo-header, the method checks if it is a connection-specific header or if it is the \"TE\" header w"
